nsions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), pi packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- When working on pi topics, read the docs and examples, and follow .md cross-references before implementing\n- Always read pi .md files completely and follow links to related docs (e.g., tui.md for TUI API details)\n</docs>\n\n<cwd>\n/tmp/endo-experiment-5c78d675047f/scratch/work\n</cwd>"},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"src/client.js is a small HTTP client wrapper. Add response caching to it, following the rules below, without breaking what it already does. Run the tests with: node --test. Do not change any file under test/.\n\n`createClient({ fetchImpl, now, ttlMs })` returns `{ get, clear, stats }`. `fetchImpl(url)` returns a promise of `{ status, body }`, and `now()` returns the current time in milliseconds.\n\nRules:\nR1. `ttlMs` is an optional option. A missing `ttlMs`, or `undefined`, means `0`. Any other value must be an integer of 0 or more, otherwise `createClient` throws a `RangeError` (that includes `null`, a string and `NaN`). With `ttlMs: 0` nothing is ever stored in the cache.\nR2. `get(url)` calls `fetchImpl` with the URL with any `#fragment` removed, and returns `{ status, body }`. A response with a status from 200 to 299 is stored in the cache under the URL without its fragment, stamped with the value of `now()` read right after `fetchImpl` resolves. While `now() - stamp < ttlMs`, a call to `get` for the same URL (fragment ignored) returns the stored response and does not call `fetchImpl`. At `now() - stamp >= ttlMs` the entry is expired: it is removed and the URL is fetched again.\nR3. A response with any other status is returned but never stored. If `fetchImpl` rejects, `get` rejects with the same error and nothing is stored.\nR4. While a fetch for a URL is in progress, other calls to `get` for the same URL (fragment ignored) wait for that fetch and get its result (or its rejection) instead of starting another one. This holds whatever `ttlMs` is. Once the fetch has finished, the next call starts afresh.\nR5. `get(url, { fresh: true })` never reads the cache and never waits for a fetch already in progress: it always calls `fetchImpl`. If the response is a 2xx one it replaces the stored entry (when `ttlMs > 0`); otherwise the stored entry is left alone.\nR6. `clear(url)` removes the stored entry for that URL (fragment ignored), and `clear()` with no argument removes every entry. Neither affects fetches in progress or the statistics. `stats()` returns a new object `{ hits, misses, fetches }`: `hits` counts the calls of `get` answered from the cache, `misses` counts every other call of `get` that got past the URL check (including `fresh` calls and calls that waited for a fetch in progress), and `fetches` counts the calls made to `fetchImpl`.\nR7. A response returned by `get` is a deep copy: changing anything inside it, at any depth (its `status`, its `body`, or anything within the `body`), must not change what is stored or what any other caller received, including callers that shared the same fetch. The URL check from before stays: a `url` that is not a non-empty string throws a `TypeError` (as a rejected promise, since `get` is async).\n\nWhen all the rules hold, reply with the single word: done"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"reasoning_content":"First, let's start by reading the existing files to understand the current state.\n","tool_calls":[{"id":"A3iCJZb58QlDWFhttO8gOjXR0hGCTiS6","type":"function","function":{"name":"read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"src/client.js\"}"